@@ -171,6 +171,16 @@ curl -X POST http://localhost:8080/action/arm
 
 ## Troubleshooting
 
+**`make up-sim-camera` takes very long or never finishes**:
+- *The image build hangs at the Intel GPU repository step.* On a corporate network whose `NO_PROXY` lists `intel.com`,
+  `repositories.intel.com` was fetched directly (it is on the public internet) and hung for many minutes. The
+  `px4-sim` Dockerfile now takes `intel.com` out of `no_proxy` for that layer and gives up after about a minute; if it
+  still fails, check that `HTTPS_PROXY` reaches `https://repositories.intel.com/gpu/intel-graphics.key`
+  (`curl -I --proxy $HTTPS_PROXY ...`). The first build compiles PX4 from source (about 15 minutes); later builds use the cache.
+- *`px4-gazebo` keeps restarting with `Failed to download model` from `fuel.gazebosim.org`.* The default world downloads
+  its models from Gazebo Fuel, which is not reachable from every network (HTTP 502 through the proxy). Use
+  `make up-sim-camera-offline`, which runs the same cameras in the self-contained `detection_zone` world.
+
 **USB camera not found** — verify your device path and update `.env`:
 ```bash
 v4l2-ctl --list-devices
diff --git a/uav-mission-compute-sdk/infra/px4-sim/Dockerfile b/uav-mission-compute-sdk/infra/px4-sim/Dockerfile
index 7f8f156..4a0e55e 100644
--- a/uav-mission-compute-sdk/infra/px4-sim/Dockerfile
+++ b/uav-mission-compute-sdk/infra/px4-sim/Dockerfile
@@ -33,8 +33,14 @@ RUN --mount=type=cache,target=/var/cache/apt,sharing=locked \
          echo "http_proxy=${http_proxy}"   >> /etc/wgetrc; \
          echo "use_proxy=on"               >> /etc/wgetrc; \
        fi \
-    && wget -qO - https://repositories.intel.com/gpu/intel-graphics.key \
-       | gpg --dearmor -o /usr/share/keyrings/intel-graphics.gpg \
+    # repositories.intel.com is on the public internet and is reached through the proxy. A corporate no_proxy that
+    # lists intel.com makes wget and apt connect directly, which hangs the build for many minutes (the Makefile passes
+    # a no_proxy without intel.com to the build, see PX4_BUILD_NO_PROXY). Here, as a second guard, take intel.com out
+    # of no_proxy for this layer and let the download fail within a minute or so instead of hanging.
+    && export no_proxy="$(printf '%s' "${no_proxy}" | tr ',' '\n' | grep -viE '^[.]?([a-z0-9-]+[.])*intel[.]com$' | paste -sd, -)" \
+    && export NO_PROXY="${no_proxy}" \
+    && wget --timeout=30 --tries=3 -qO /tmp/intel-graphics.key https://repositories.intel.com/gpu/intel-graphics.key \
+    && gpg --dearmor -o /usr/share/keyrings/intel-graphics.gpg /tmp/intel-graphics.key \
     && echo "deb [arch=amd64 signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/intel-graphics.gpg] \
        https://repositories.intel.com/gpu/ubuntu noble unified" \
        > /etc/apt/sources.list.d/intel-gpu.list \
